Dock keystone: windows tagged "dock" (features/sidedock) render as a perspective
trapezoid with rounded, anti-aliased corners, a warped drop shadow and frosted
blur that follow it, and input mapped back through the inverse warp.

From sihooleebd/nixos (features/hyprland/trapezoid.patch at 0a7686c, "dock fix",
which added keystone_rounding / keystone_shadow_* / keystone_parallax and fixed
fractional scale), regenerated against this flake's patched Hyprland. Two local
changes on top. First, ksDockKeystone also runs the window box through renderModif, as
the surface box already is, so the warp stays on the window during workspace
slides and zoom.
Second, the move gesture, started on a dock pile card, moves just that card
horizontally under the finger (live, like moving a floating window) and on
release runs `gestures:dock_swipe_exec <l|r|none> <front>`, which
features/sidedock points at `dock.sh gesture-move` to cycle or spring back. One
gesture rather than a second 3-finger one: Hyprland runs only the first gesture
matching a finger count.
Third, scale-to-fit (CWindow::fitTransform): a window tagged `fit`, and every
dock card, whose client does not follow its configured size (Waydroid's fixed
Android display) is drawn scaled into its box, aspect kept and centred, instead
of cropped. Covers the surface tree's texture boxes and UVs, pointer / touch /
tablet input (mapped back through the same scale; the letterbox margin is a
miss) and commit damage (repaints the whole window). Inactive while the client's
size matches, so well-behaved windows render 1:1 exactly as before.
Fourth, two dock-card render fixes on top of upstream's warp: the drop shadow is
no longer clipped to the window's FLAT box (that left a shadow whose inner edge
was the straight flat-box edge, not the trapezoid's; the shader's own cutout is
warped and suffices), and the frosted-blur pass samples the blurred framebuffer
at each fragment's screen position (ksScreenUV) instead of the flat box's UVs,
so the blur behind a tilted card is the blur of what is really behind it.

